{# WHAT RUNS WHERE — every area of the installation against every module it
   could run.

   AN AREA THAT RUNS NOTHING IS THE POINT OF THE TABLE. It reports nothing
   anywhere else in the product, precisely because it has no module to report
   through, so this is the only place it can be seen — which is why the empty
   rows stay and are drawn quiet rather than filtered out.

   THE SAME TABLE ON TWO SCREENS, because it is the same fact: the
   installation screen asks it as "what runs where" and the modules screen
   asks it as "the catalogue". Two queries for it would be two answers with no
   way to say which was right. #}
{%- if matrix.rows is empty -%}
    <p class="use">No area is registered here yet, so there is nothing to run a module in.</p>
{%- else -%}
    <table class="tbl">
        <tr>
            <th>area</th>
            {%- for column in matrix.columns %}<th>{{ column.label|lower }}</th>{% endfor -%}
            <th>zones</th>
            <th>state</th>
        </tr>
        {%- for row in matrix.rows -%}
            <tr>
                <td{{ row.isLive ? '' : ' class="fog"' }}><b>{{ row.name }}</b></td>
                {%- for column in matrix.columns -%}
                    {%- set on = row.running[column.slug]|default(false) -%}
                    <td class="{{ on ? 'g' : 'fog' }}">{{ on ? 'on' : 'off' }}</td>
                {%- endfor -%}
                <td class="{{ row.zones ? 'g' : 'fog' }}">{{ row.zones is null ? '—' : row.zones }}</td>
                <td><span class="chip {{ row.isLive ? 'ok' : 'idle' }}">{{ row.isLive ? 'live' : 'awaiting setup' }}</span></td>
            </tr>
        {%- endfor -%}
    </table>
{%- endif -%}
